      Green Glue Damping vs. Mass Loaded Vinyl (MLV) Soundproofing
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      When designing a soundproof partition wall or ceiling, builders face a classic dilemma between two premier acoustic technologies: <strong>Green Glue Viscoelastic Damping Compound</strong> and <strong>Mass Loaded Vinyl (MLV)</strong>. While both dramatically improve Sound Transmission Class (STC) ratings, they operate on completely different acoustic principles—one relies on shear friction damping, while the other relies on limp deadweight mass.
    </p>

