    title="Why Using Both MLV and Green Glue Together is Usually a Waste of Money"
    note="A common misconception among high-budget home theater builders is thinking: 'If Green Glue is great, and MLV is great, doing both must be twice as good!' In practice, layering MLV directly under a Green Glue drywall sandwich offers diminishing acoustic returns. The rigid drywall sheets clamp the flexible MLV so tightly against the studs that the vinyl loses its limp mass decoupling freedom. You spend an extra $2.00 per square foot for a negligible 1 to 2 STC point gain! If you have extra budget, invest that money in RESILIENT SOUND ISOLATION CLIPS (such as GenieClips or WhisperClips with 25-gauge hat channel) to physically decouple the drywall framing from the studs. A decoupled wall with Green Glue delivers an astonishing STC 60+, which stops heavy subwoofer bass vibrations cold."
